# Code identity of the X570 tree that ran the step-level co-run sweep on
# gfx1201
#
# Captured 2026-09-04, after Experiment C run 2 finished at 160/160 and
# before this sweep started. Four files were synced in beforehand; every
# other file is as expC run 2 left it, and in particular
# src/burstserve/runtime.py is still 139b944^ -- before the
# max_steps_per_round flag -- which is the pin that keeps every hardware
# campaign here commensurable. This sweep does not use the runtime at
# all.
#
# What this sweep exists to settle. On 2026-09-04 the whole-call co-run
# harness was shown to charge `hipMalloc`-class device drains as
# contention: a mismatched pair that reads 7.3x through it reads 0.995
# when the same masks are stepped on resident adapters, and the step
# series resolved the difference into one device drain per step, exactly
# one peer step long. On gfx90a the damage is confined to NARROW slices
# -- 13+91 reads 1.3559 whole-call and 0.998 stepped, while 91+13 reads
# 1.0317 and 1.031 -- and gfx1201's table has never been checked.
#
# Two things turn on it. `docs/prereg-intra-tenant.md` charged its
# four-way arrangement 1.297, which is a PAIR at 16+16, and said in the
# document that this stand-in was the number its prediction turned on;
# expC has now returned verdict 3 with c2 dominating c4, which is what
# 1.11 predicts, but 1.11 is a gfx90a measurement. And 3.8's gfx1201 row
# reads externality(8, 24) = 1.3383, a narrow-slice entry, for the tenant
# that paces the round.
#
# Files synced in from dd immediately before this capture:
#   scripts/run_amd_nway_steps.py      new -- the step-level N-way harness
#   scripts/campaign_nway_steps.sh     new -- this sweep
#   scripts/summarise_nway_steps.py    new -- its analysis
#   scripts/run_amd_mismatched_corun.py  gains --full-die, default 32, so
#                                      gfx1201 behaviour is unchanged
#   scripts/run_amd_matrix_cell.py     _grant_shapes is tenant-ordered
#                                      now. Held back all through expC on
#                                      purpose; expC's shapes are
#                                      width-sorted and its attestation
#                                      says so.
#
# The adapters, executor, masked_streams and provenance hash IDENTICALLY
# to DiamondHill's copies, so the two architectures' step-level tables
# are produced by the same code and not merely by the same procedure.
